{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/172077-court-of-solstice-culture","id":172077,"title":"Court of Solstice Culture","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-17T15:37:25-07:00","id":172077,"title":"Court of Solstice Culture","content":"Inspired by the entitlement of same name (found in Lords of Summer), I wrote this way back when to help spring-board ideas for people who wanted to make the court officially part of the seasonal freehold. Tell me what you think:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Court of inbetween is not so much a court as it is a noble order. However, they also act as keepers to the crown of seasons. When a monarch acts against the wishes of the freehold's need to pass on the crown to the next season, the Court of Solstice acts as both mediator and law against refusal, allying itself to any (and sometimes all) resistances that would wish the corrupt monarch to step down.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Besides royalty, the Court is more-or-less focused on one thing: Clarity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Since its admittance into the freehold system, the Court of Solstice has held it in their ambitions to keep the Changelings under their care from going mad. This is done through their service to the &quot;Word of Reason.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Word of Reason is not a god, nor a pantheon, but rather a philosophy (that usually conjoins with that of any given religion a changeling may already have) that states that a changeling is of two parents: the mortal realm, and fae dominion. To reject either is to cast aside a part of a changeling's heritage. Even if not a natural heredity, the Word of Reason states that in order to surpass the tragedy of change, one must accept it (embracing is optional, but acceptance if the first step to better clarity.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Because both sides of the Changeling exist as they do, Clerics of Equinox focus their attention in therapeutic practices, as well as desiring balance in all things they commit to. They see mortals and changelings as family, and will even aid those who are not of faery, but are under psychological delusion, thus attempting to weaken the suffering of the mind, which the court knows all too well to be a terrible torture.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Word of Reason holds the following as tenants:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I. Thou shalt hold to thy kin and people.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">II. Thou shalt not commit actions of madness or Contract with Lunacy, and if so, thou shall redeem thyself and remedy thy victim with the gift of Reason.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">III. Thou shalt yield to the power of word, and shield thyself with the power of sword as last resort.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">IV. Thou shalt forgive with time's passage, and bitter wisdom.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">V. Thou shalt not kill save against those who would torment the weak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Naturally, the court is affectionate to those who learn medical abilities, contracts of Lucidity and Hours, and hold in high reverence one who can turn a loyalist or fetch to the side of the freehold. However, those who are known to cause madness through the contracts of the moon, or through other means are considered with contempt, only being forgiven if proven to have made good on remedying the madness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>View points on the other courts:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Spring: Flighty and whimsical, but perhaps their desire can go too far in times of peace?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Summer: Too quick to attack, too paranoid at people's hidden malevolence, and too unforgiving towards even the innocent.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Autumn: Fear is poison to the soul, what are you once even that is too intoxicated to cure?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Winter: They understand necessity, but their secretive nature only worsens their ability to live the normal lives they seek.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Court Hierarchy:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Courtier/Pilgrim of Solstice* -&gt; Acolyte of Solstice** -&gt; Priest of Solstice*** -&gt; Bishop of Solstice**** -&gt; Archbishop of Solstice*****</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Alternate roles within Solstice:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Ambassador of the Between, Confessor of the Mad, The Peace Keeper, Equinox Pilgrim.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A Courtier of Solstice need not be a servant to the cloth, and is simply a member of the court's &quot;peasantry.&quot; However, to gain rank in Solstice, you must willing to accept similar duties found within Clerical systems. The Passion of Solstice is Desperation (no joke)). The mein of a Solstice Courtier is neutral as it is balanced in being not too much one thing or the other, and a sense of grounding can be felt by those of stronger connection to the Court of inbetween. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Blessing: Feast of the Scraps</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Since Solstice and Equinox aren't long enough periods within the year to be as powerful or important as an actual season, Courtiers of Solstice are unable to gain contracts based on their court, not are they allowed to gain contracts connected to the other seasons. However, Desperation is a mixture of Fear, Desire, Wrath and Sorrow all in one, and so is it that Solstice Changelings are able to harvest twice as much glamour from people under this special type of emotion. What's more, they may incite bedlam based upon it (if they have enough Wyrd). </span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Other Courts:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Spring: They're nice, but they don't give themselves much to go on, to the point of being stuck up about it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Summer: If they had their way, they'd have us all trying to shake hands with the gentry, or be slaughtered from behind by false conversions from the Fetches and Loyalists.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Autumn: They attempt to balance, yet would have us restrain from our own passion and purpose as a court.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Winter: Let them deal with the mad, they will either cure them, or learn from their failings.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}